            <ArticleTitle>Copper-catalyzed asymmetric sp3 C-H arylation of tetrahydroisoquinoline mediated by a visible light photoredox catalyst.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2636-2643</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3762/bjoc.12.260</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This report describes a highly enantioselective oxidative sp3 C-H arylation of N-aryltetrahydroisoquinolines (THIQs) through a dual catalysis platform. The combination of the photoredox catalyst, [Ir(ppy)2(dtbbpy)]PF6, and chiral copper catalysts provide a mild and highly effective sp3 C-H asymmetric arylation of THIQs.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
